Z||000000||MR2KLR||11-13-2001||07:41 PM||||<BR>any idea what it would sound like? I know it is short 2 pistons but would it sound more powerfull? the 2.5L is only .3L short of a 2.8L. I put a stock 2M6 exhaust on my old 2M4 and it was silet. I want some grumbling back there I'm already planing on useing a 2.5" straight pipe in place of the cat and 2.5" stainless the rest of the way back to some new fiero store 2M6 tips.<P> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Exhaust/West_Coast_Muffler_sound.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Exhaust/West_Coast_Muffler_sound.html</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||11-13-2001||08:16 PM||||I have 2.5 inch on my V6 and it worked out great. But on a 2.5?  <P>On my old 87 coupe I had the Header, straight pipe going through a Dynomax (the stock muffler didn't last long after the header and straight pipe.) and it sounded great! Gave it a nice snarl that sounded more V6 to those not knowledgable. Its been a long time since it was totaled and I miss it. Try taking off the cat and put in your "test pipe" and see what you think of the sound. You could probably tune the sound a bit with the West's muffler. <P>We have a Pace car in the club that went to V6 exhaust, straight pipe and header and that car always sounded good. <P>I would be concerned how much you would lose on the bottom end with the bigger pipe. Sure, there isn't much anyway but you don't want to lose anymore!||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-13-2001||10:07 PM||||I put about 100-200 miles on my old 84 SE with a Straight down tube out in front of the rear wheel. While I waited on the 2M6 exhaust to get here.  It was like I had a whole new car alot more rev happy. and more fun to drive if you ask me.<P>what header was that Indy useing?||||reg||1
